{"id":"u-9b1f40ce-12bf-49d4-8cfc-3cd5907056b6","src":"community","title":"5/3/1 Athletic Build","author":"Anonymous","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/sMqJNB-531-athletic-build-1","desc":"A 5-day powerbuilding program for intermediate to advanced lifters chasing a lean, proportional physique alongside continued strength development on the main barbell lifts.\n\nThe program runs 5/3/1 progression on bench, squat, deadlift, and overhead press, with opposite-lift BBB volume on upper days. Accessories target common aesthetic weak points: direct chest work (pressing + isolation) for pec development, lateral raises across three sessions for V-taper, and dedicated rear delt and rotator cuff work for shoulder health and balance.\n\nLower days focus on strength rather than hypertrophy, with rotating accessory pairings to vary stimulus across cycles. Targeted glute and abductor work is included for hip development beyond what the main compound lifts provide. Wednesday acts as a lighter buffer day between the two lower sessions: a chest pressing slot, back volume, direct arm work, and rear delts.\n\nCore training and cardio (incline walking or stairmaster) are performed daily outside of gym sessions and are not programmed in this template.\n\n**Progression & stalling**\n\nSet your training max (TM) at 85% of a current estimated 1RM (best AMRAP set: weight × reps × 0.0333 + weight). All percentages run off the TM, never your true max. After each 3-week cycle plus deload: add 2.5 kg to bench/OHP TMs and 5 kg to squat/deadlift TMs.\n\nIf progressing too fast (AMRAP sets exceeding ~8–10 reps on the 1+ week), do not skip ahead — keep the standard TM increments and let the rep PRs accumulate. The TM is meant to stay conservative.\n\nIf you stall (missing prescribed reps or grinding the top set for 2+ cycles on a lift), reset that lift's TM to 85% of its current value and rebuild. Reset only the stalled lift, not all four. Optionally progress BBB weight across cycles (50% → 55% → 60%) as long as all 5×10 sets are completed cleanly.","level":["Intermediate","Advanced"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength","Athletics"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":2,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-08-21T17:39:30.452Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Day 1","Day 2","Day 3","Day 4","Day 5"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"pct":65},{"r":5,"pct":75},{"r":5,"pct":85}]},{"n":"Overhead Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"pct":50,"x":5}]},{"n":"Wide Grip Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Chest Supported Row (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Face Pull","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":20,"rpe":6,"rpeHi":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":20,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Incline Chest Fly (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":7,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"pct":65},{"r":5,"pct":75},{"r":5,"pct":85}]},{"n":"Hack Squat","sets":[{"lo":5,"hi":6,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Leg Curl","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Bulgarian Split Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hip Abductor (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":20,"rpe":6,"rpeHi":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Standing Calf Raise","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":7,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Dip (Weighted)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Pull-Up (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Bicep Curl (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Rear Delt Fly (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":20,"rpe":6,"rpeHi":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":20,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Overhead Extension (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"pct":65},{"r":5,"pct":75},{"r":